@startuml
title 3.16.12 Create a donation campaign
caption UC-159 | Planned | Proposed design
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor white
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
show footbox
<style>
lifeLine {
    LineStyle 0
}
</style>
skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor white
    ActorBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBackgroundColor white
    LifeLineBorderColor black
    GroupBackgroundColor white
    GroupHeaderBackgroundColor white
}

' Source: docs/requirements/uc.md
' Main entity migration: No migration: proposed entity only
' One-table abstraction: related repository reads/writes stay inside the service.
actor "Admin" as Actor
participant "Donation Campaign UI (proposed)" as Page
participant "Campaign API (proposed)" as API
participant "Campaign Service (proposed)" as Service
participant "donation_campaigns" as Table <<proposed entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Create a donation campaign
activate Page
Page -> Page: 2: Enter name, receiving organization, schedule and eligibility rules
Page -> API: 3: Create donation campaign (proposed interface)
activate API
API -> API: 4: Authenticate active session and require ADMIN role
alt Session and required permission are valid
    API -> API: 5: Proposed: validate required fields, time window and eligibility\nrules
    alt Request input is valid
        API -> Service: 6: Create a donation campaign for the current actor
        activate Service
        Service -> Service: 7: Check campaign policy and receiving organization (proposed)
        alt Campaign information is valid
            Service -> Service: 8: Begin proposed transaction
            Service -> Table: 9: Insert proposed campaign with creation metadata
            activate Table
            Table --> Service: 10: Proposed campaign id
            deactivate Table
            Service -> Service: 11: Record initial change history and audit; commit
            Service --> API: 12: Created campaign (proposed)
            API --> Page: 13: HTTP 201 (proposed): Created campaign (proposed)
            Page --> Actor: 14: Display campaign without assigning or disposing items
        else Missing fields, invalid schedule or incompatible rules
            Service --> API: 8.1: Invalid campaign information
            API --> Page: 8.2: HTTP 422 (proposed)
            Page --> Actor: 8.3: Display error; do not report success
        end
        deactivate Service
    else Invalid request input
        API --> Page: 6.1: Proposed validation error response
        Page --> Actor: 6.2: Display validation errors; do not execute the operation
    end
else Missing/invalid session or required permission
    API --> Page: 5.1: Proposed authentication/access error response
    Page --> Actor: 5.2: Show session or access error; no protected result
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend bottom left
PLANNED: API/UI and donation_campaigns table are proposed, not present in the runtime or migrations.
Required schema and policy design remain open.
endlegend

@enduml
